### GET request to example server
GET https://examples.http-client.intellij.net/get
    ?generated-in=IntelliJ IDEA

###
### Register a new user
POST http://localhost:8080/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Arliner Test",
  "email": "arline@test123.com",
  "password": "testpass123"
}

### Try registering the SAME email again — should fail with 409
POST http://localhost:8080/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Arline Test",
  "email": "arline@test.com",
  "password": "testpass123"
}

### Login with correct credentials
POST http://localhost:8080/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "arline@test.com",
  "password": "testpass123"
}

### Login with WRONG password — should fail with 401
POST http://localhost:8080/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "arline@test.com",
  "password": "wrongpassword"
}

### Protected endpoint WITH a valid token — paste your real access token below
GET http://localhost:8080/api/test
Authorization: Bearer
eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9.eyJzdWIiOiJhcmxpbmVAdGVzdDEyMy5jb20iLCJpYXQiOjE3ODc0MjUyMjMsImV4cCI6MTc4NzQyNjEyM30.-fjhRBOudZsfUaBlA8dYgWP-1fCgK256TFoqTGYb-l4

### Protected endpoint with NO token — should fail with 401/403
GET http://localhost:8080/api/test

### Protected endpoint with a garbage/malformed token — should fail cleanly
GET http://localhost:8080/api/test
Authorization: Bearer garbage.invalid.token

### Refresh — paste your real refresh token below
POST http://localhost:8080/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

"PASTE_REFRESH_TOKEN_HERE"
